1
00:00:00,080 --> 00:00:02,400
The Gurkha Contingent:

2
00:00:02,480 --> 00:00:06,875
Singapore's Neutral Force, 1949 to 1965

3
00:00:06,875 --> 00:00:10,846
In February 1949 an
officer of the Singapore

4
00:00:10,926 --> 00:00:14,344
police flew to New Delhi to bring back

5
00:00:14,424 --> 00:00:18,475
148 Gurkhas recruited
in the hills of Nepal.

6
00:00:18,475 --> 00:00:22,124
They were to form a new riot
squad, replacing the Sikh

7
00:00:22,204 --> 00:00:25,921
contingent that had kept
order in Singapore since 1881,

8
00:00:26,001 --> 00:00:30,340
and they were valued for one
quality above all: they belonged to

9
00:00:30,420 --> 00:00:34,425
none of the communities they
might be called on to police.

10
00:00:34,425 --> 00:00:38,099
Within two years that quality
was tested in the worst

11
00:00:38,179 --> 00:00:42,349
communal riots Singapore had
seen, and the Gurkha Contingent

12
00:00:42,429 --> 00:00:45,900
has been part of the
Singapore police ever since.

13
00:00:45,900 --> 00:00:51,531
The Sikh Police Contingent was
disbanded after the Japanese occupation,

14
00:00:51,611 --> 00:00:53,864
and the independence of India

15
00:00:53,944 --> 00:00:57,725
in 1947 changed where
the colony could recruit.

16
00:00:57,725 --> 00:01:01,601
The Britain–India–Nepal
agreement of 1947 divided the

17
00:01:01,681 --> 00:01:05,408
Gurkha regiments of the
old Indian Army between the

18
00:01:05,488 --> 00:01:09,065
Indian Army and the British
Army, and the British

19
00:01:09,145 --> 00:01:13,250
looked to Gurkhas to fill
the place the Sikhs had left.

20
00:01:13,250 --> 00:01:17,040
The National Library Board's
account notes that Gurkhas

21
00:01:17,120 --> 00:01:20,839
had already proved themselves
in the defence of Malaya

22
00:01:20,919 --> 00:01:25,000
during the war, and describes
them as impartial but loyal.

23
00:01:25,000 --> 00:01:29,535
The Straits Times of the 16th
of February 1949 carried the

24
00:01:29,615 --> 00:01:34,150
news under the headline "Gurkhas
to form new riot squad."

25
00:01:34,150 --> 00:01:38,676
It reported that R. A. H. Cowan,
an assistant superintendent

26
00:01:38,756 --> 00:01:43,358
in the police communications
division, had flown to New Delhi

27
00:01:43,438 --> 00:01:48,118
and would bring back 148 Gurkhas
recruited in Nepal to replace

28
00:01:48,198 --> 00:01:52,650
the Sikh contingent as the
police riot squad in Singapore.

29
00:01:52,650 --> 00:01:57,260
The men and most of their
families were to be housed in 12

30
00:01:57,340 --> 00:02:01,626
blocks of new quarters on
Duxton Plain, off Neil Road,

31
00:02:01,706 --> 00:02:06,800
built at a cost of $490,000 on
a site of five and a half acres.

32
00:02:06,800 --> 00:02:10,788
The paper also recalled that
during the occupation the

33
00:02:10,868 --> 00:02:15,459
Japanese had used Sikh policemen
as guards for prisoner-of-war

34
00:02:15,539 --> 00:02:19,075
and civilian internment
camps, and that the Sikh

35
00:02:19,155 --> 00:02:23,675
contingent had been disbanded
soon after liberation in 1945.

36
00:02:23,675 --> 00:02:27,612
The Gurkha Contingent
was formed as part of the

37
00:02:27,692 --> 00:02:31,202
Singapore police on the 9th of April 1949,

38
00:02:31,282 --> 00:02:36,325
with 142 men who had served as
Gurkhas in the British Army.

39
00:02:36,325 --> 00:02:39,562
Its first commanding
officer, according to the

40
00:02:39,642 --> 00:02:43,175
National Library Board,
was Major Scott Leathart.

41
00:02:43,175 --> 00:02:46,850
Its first real test came within two years.

42
00:02:46,850 --> 00:02:50,583
On the 2nd of December 1950
the High Court ruled on

43
00:02:50,663 --> 00:02:54,395
the disputed custody of
Maria Hertogh, a Dutch girl

44
00:02:54,475 --> 00:02:57,759
who had been raised by
a Malay Muslim family,

45
00:02:57,839 --> 00:03:02,325
and on the 11th of December
riots broke out across the city.

46
00:03:02,325 --> 00:03:07,128
The Straits Times of the 13th of
December reported that the death

47
00:03:07,208 --> 00:03:12,162
toll had reached 16, with more than
180 people treated in hospital,

48
00:03:12,242 --> 00:03:17,200
and described a dawn-to-dusk curfew
enforced by troops and police.

49
00:03:17,200 --> 00:03:20,304
Its reporters wrote that
"hundreds of British,

50
00:03:20,384 --> 00:03:23,775
Gurkha and Malay troops
patrolled empty streets."

51
00:03:23,775 --> 00:03:27,631
The paper did not separate
the police contingent from the

52
00:03:27,711 --> 00:03:31,291
army's Gurkha units, but
the National Library Board's

53
00:03:31,371 --> 00:03:35,503
account names the Maria Hertogh
riots as one of the occasions

54
00:03:35,583 --> 00:03:39,450
on which the Gurkha Contingent's
impartiality was shown.

55
00:03:39,450 --> 00:03:43,550
The same reasoning
applied through the 1950s.

56
00:03:43,550 --> 00:03:47,605
The contingent was used
again during the Hock Lee bus

57
00:03:47,685 --> 00:03:52,365
strike and riots of 1955 and
during the Chinese middle-school

58
00:03:52,445 --> 00:03:56,500
unrest of the same decade,
and it is also recorded as

59
00:03:56,580 --> 00:04:00,950
having been deployed in the
communal riots of July 1964.

60
00:04:00,950 --> 00:04:03,918
Lee Kuan Yew later explained the value

61
00:04:03,998 --> 00:04:06,725
of that neutrality in his memoirs.

62
00:04:06,725 --> 00:04:11,687
Using Chinese policemen against Malays,
or Malay policemen against Chinese,

63
00:04:11,767 --> 00:04:15,048
he wrote, would have had
widespread repercussions,

64
00:04:15,128 --> 00:04:18,825
whereas "the Gurkhas, on the
other hand, were neutral."

65
00:04:18,825 --> 00:04:22,301
When Singapore became independent in 1965,

66
00:04:22,381 --> 00:04:26,700
it kept the contingent as
part of its police force.

67
00:04:26,700 --> 00:04:31,575
The contingent remains a unit
of the Singapore Police Force.

68
00:04:31,575 --> 00:04:37,083
According to the National Library Board
and the government's SG101 resource,

69
00:04:37,163 --> 00:04:39,436
its members come to Singapore at

70
00:04:39,516 --> 00:04:43,994
around 18 and return to Nepal
after 15 to 20 years of service,

71
00:04:44,074 --> 00:04:47,082
living in the meantime in a self-contained

72
00:04:47,162 --> 00:04:51,500
cantonment at Mount Vernon with
its own temple and schools.

73
00:04:51,500 --> 00:04:57,395
It guards selected installations, augments
the police at major security events,

74
00:04:57,475 --> 00:05:00,500
and serves as a counter-terrorism force.

75
00:05:00,500 --> 00:05:05,024
Where it fits in the bigger story:
The Gurkha Contingent was created

76
00:05:05,104 --> 00:05:09,289
to solve a specific problem that
the end of the Sikh contingent

77
00:05:09,369 --> 00:05:13,825
had left behind: how to keep order
in a city of several communities

78
00:05:13,905 --> 00:05:17,900
without the police being seen
to take one community's side.

79
00:05:17,900 --> 00:05:22,373
Its value was tested in 1950,
within two years of its formation,

80
00:05:22,453 --> 00:05:27,354
and the decisions made then about
who should police a divided city are

81
00:05:27,434 --> 00:05:32,049
part of the reason a small force
recruited from the hills of Nepal

82
00:05:32,129 --> 00:05:36,825
is still part of Singapore's police
more than seventy years later.
